MID_SC12_00_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_00_m01_001: Now...let us dance.
MID_SC12_00_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_00_m02_001: I do not know your magic. Who are you?
MID_SC12_00_m02_002: First we dispense of them. Then we become\nacquainted.
MID_SC12_00_m02_003: Very well.
MID_SC12_00_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_00_m03_001: Allow me to demonstrate the difference between\nhumans and beasts.
MID_SC12_00_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_00_m04_001: How does the blood of this land taste, Answerer?
MID_SC12_00_m04_002: This man holds tremendous power. It puts me in\nmind of Fódlan's 10...
MID_SC12_00_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_00_m05_001: Who are you? So...strong...
MID_SC12_00_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_00_e02_001: I can support you with magic. You may rely on me\nfor healing as well.
MID_SC12_01_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_m01_001: Why did you save me?
MID_SC12_01_m01_002: Because I could. I was taken by the fierce light in\nyour eyes.
MID_SC12_01_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_m02_001: Aren't you going to scurry off?
MID_SC12_01_m02_002: Are you kidding? This is my chance to get revenge\nfor my dad!
MID_SC12_01_m02_003: You won't escape. I'll take you down with my own\ntwo hands!
MID_SC12_01_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_m03_001: Brrgh!
MID_SC12_01_m03_002: Roar all you like! I'll shut you up soon enough!
MID_SC12_01_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_m04_001: Brrrgh!
MID_SC12_01_m04_002: Yes... Cry out! Reveal your truth to me!
MID_SC12_01_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_m05_001: Brgh!
MID_SC12_01_m05_002: What have I gotten myself into now, hunting a\ncreature like this. Honestly.
MID_SC12_01_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_m06_001: Are you telling me it's still got the strength to fight?
MID_SC12_01_m06_002: Formidable creature. I am amazed at the fortitude of\nthese feral beasts.
MID_SC12_01_m06_003: I too.
MID_SC12_01_e01: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_e01_001: That big one, Redears—that's the sea beast that got\nmy dad! But damn, it's so far off!
MID_SC12_01_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_e03_001: Oh, no! There's more of them!
MID_SC12_01_e03_002: Over there, I see.
MID_SC12_01_e04: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_e04_001: Yet more lurk? What fun.
MID_SC12_01_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_01_e05_001: Now I'm ready! Get in my way, and you'll pay\nthe price!
MID_BD12_02_m01: <TH>
MID_BD12_02_m01_001: Get 'em, everybody! Come on! Let's show 'em\nwho's boss!
MID_BD12_02_m01_002: Fools who do not fear the spirits will be made to\nrepent by force!
MID_BD12_02_m02: <TH>
MID_BD12_02_m02_001: What is that sword? It's freakish!
MID_BD12_02_m02_002: Is it an Arc? From the temples? Who is this guy?
MID_BD12_02_m03: <TH>
MID_BD12_02_m03_001: I've never seen magic like this... It is unnatural!
MID_BD12_02_m03_002: Perhaps this will serve as an educational opportunity\nfor you then. I suggest you take it!
MID_BD12_02_m04: <TH>
MID_BD12_02_m04_001: Ridiculous... How can I...
MID_SC12_03_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m01_001: Eliminate the intruders. Eliminate the intruders.
MID_SC12_03_m01_002: This facility is well equipped for defense, but that\nmust be a finite resource.
MID_SC12_03_m01_003: It is simple. We will cut down all that approach.
MID_SC12_03_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m02_001: Who are they?
MID_SC12_03_m02_002: Anyone affiliated with Vritra is an enemy. All\nenemies will be eliminated!
MID_SC12_03_m02_003: I can't even tell what's going on, and now we've got\nto deal with these people—whoever they are!
MID_SC12_03_m02_004: Indeed we must. And it does not appear they are in\nthe mood for a conversation.
MID_SC12_03_m02_005: You clod! You got us into this mess—so you had\nbetter get us out of it!
MID_SC12_03_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m03_001: Show me how you dance, woman in white!
MID_SC12_03_m03_002: This man has an intense blood lust... But who is he?
MID_SC12_03_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m04_001: I have seen equipment like this before...
MID_SC12_03_m04_002: Well-disguised, but they appear to be outfitted like\nthe sailors.
MID_SC12_03_m04_003: What curiosities these handheld cannons are. I am\nshocked that they still function.
MID_SC12_03_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m05_001: Vritra is unforgivable! I will protect Kunlun's secrets\nwith my life.
MID_SC12_03_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m06_001: I believe I have some understanding of who you\npeople may be.
MID_SC12_03_m06_002: I'm sure we'd love to hear what you have to say once\nwe've bound and gagged you.
MID_SC12_03_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m07_001: Don't hate us for what we have to do. Obviously we\ncan't afford to let you simply walk out of here.
MID_SC12_03_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m08_001: Ah, yeah! Now's my time to shine and show you\nwhat I'm made of.
MID_SC12_03_m09: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m09_001: Allow me to demonstrate what happens when you\nface off with Dadao the Relentless!
MID_SC12_03_m10: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m10_001: Uh oh! It's me they're after!
MID_SC12_03_m11: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_m11_001: I bear you no ill will. However I cannot abide\naffiliates of Vritra.
MID_SC12_03_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_e03_001: I feel... Is Katarina blessing me with power?
MID_SC12_03_e04: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_e04_001: These devices seem to be bolstering her strength.\n{SetColor=Gold}Shut down all three{SetColor=Default} to put a stop to that!
MID_SC12_03_e06: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_e06_001: You've only weakened my link with Katarina.\nI won't be stopped so easily.
MID_SC12_03_e08: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_e08_001: They've deactivated two of the devices? I must stop\nthem before they can do more damage.
MID_SC12_03_e11: <TH>
MID_SC12_03_e11_001: No... Katarina's power is gone!
MID_SC12_03_e11_002: The power that bolstered our opponent has\ndissipated. If we are to defeat her, the time is now!
MID_BD12_04_m01: <TH>
MID_BD12_04_m01_001: Listen up, pretty boy. You're gonna regret ever\npicking a fight with the great Majide!
MID_BD12_04_m02: <TH>
MID_BD12_04_m02_001: You know, I really hate guys like you!
MID_BD12_04_m02_002: I had thought you capable. It appears that\nI was mistaken.
MID_BD12_04_m02_003: Wh-what'd you just say?! How dare you try'n make\na fool outta me!
MID_BD12_04_m03: <TH>
MID_BD12_04_m03_001: How in the world? There's no way you can be\nthat strong!
MID_BD12_04_m04: <TH>
MID_BD12_04_m04_002: No... The great Majide fails...
MID_BD12_04_m04_001: Not just a remarkable weapon, but skill too.\nHow interesting...
MID_BD12_07_m01: <TH>
MID_BD12_07_m01_001: Come, warrior! Show me your essence!
MID_BD12_07_m01_002: Your power, your skill, your mettle... I will test it all!
MID_BD12_07_m02: <TH>
MID_BD12_07_m02_001: You are strong...stronger than any I have faced!
MID_BD12_07_m02_002: Strength like yours is wasted in a human frame.
MID_BD12_07_m03: <TH>
MID_BD12_07_m03_001: Stop, both of you. That is more than enough.
MID_SC12_08_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m01_006: For your first trial, you must deactivate the devices\nwithin the time limit.
MID_SC12_08_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m01_007: This is all a bit beyond me, but I think those are the\nthings he wants us to deactivate.
MID_SC12_08_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m01_001: What are these?
MID_SC12_08_m01_002: More phantoms? They're blocking our path to\nthe enemy!
MID_SC12_08_m01_003: They are my doing, and should be strong enough to\nbe of some aid in the battle.
MID_SC12_08_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m01_004: What? What has happened?
MID_SC12_08_m01_005: Now what? They just vanished! Some "aid in the\nbattle," Fabio!
MID_SC12_08_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m02_001: Hahahaha! Good. I will lose myself in the fray.
MID_SC12_08_m02_002: Sweetie, is it just me, or are there a LOT of them?\nThis is overkill, isn't it?
MID_SC12_08_m02_003: The megalith is vested with the personality of a\nsoldier. We should expect a more thorough defense.
MID_SC12_08_m02_004: With a reception like this, we don't have time to\nfool around.
MID_SC12_08_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m03_001: Show me your power, lightning-shrouded phantoms!\nNow!
MID_SC12_08_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_m04_001: Enough! You have demonstrated your ability.
MID_SC12_08_e01: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_e01_002: A barrier protects Hannibal. While it stands, we will\nnot be able to put a scratch on him.
MID_SC12_08_e01_003: As he says, we must hurry to {SetColor=Gold}deactivate both\ndevices{SetColor=Default}—{SetColor=Gold}before it is too late{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC12_08_e06: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_e06_002: The second trial commences. Show me that you have\nthe power to defeat us.
MID_SC12_08_e06_003: The barrier protecting Hannibal remains... Must we\nfirst {SetColor=Gold}defeat his elephant riders{SetColor=Default}?
MID_SC12_08_e07: <TH>
MID_SC12_08_e07_001: You do not have the strength. You have been found\nlacking. Leave now.
MID_SC12_09_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m01_001: I am Alexandra Tamsanqa, Silver Knight of Tellus,\nand I am ready to fight!
MID_SC12_09_m01_002: She comes across as sincere to me. But then...\nwhat's going on here?
MID_SC12_09_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m02_001: So it's true? Even on that stupid flying mount,\nshe's practically immune to arrows? Unbelievable.
MID_SC12_09_m02_002: If bows aren't the answer, I hope someone here has\na plan B.
MID_SC12_09_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m04_001: Even though these ships are not real...my mind\nreturns to that fateful night.
MID_SC12_09_m04_002: O Sea Tyrant Cetus... How I yearn to meet\nyou again, Demonic Beast.
MID_SC12_09_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m05_001: Kill... Destroy everything...
MID_SC12_09_m05_002: Tch! That was no figment of the imagination.\nI heard it, clear as day.
MID_SC12_09_m05_003: Your Majesty? Is something amiss?
MID_SC12_09_m05_004: There is no cause for alarm. I was a bit lightheaded,\nthat's all.
MID_SC12_09_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m06_001: Kill them all. Mow them down, one by one...\nUse my power.
MID_SC12_09_m06_002: That voice again...it is even clearer than last time.
MID_SC12_09_m06_003: Is it coming from...within me?
MID_SC12_09_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m07_001: I hate seeing you out here on the battlefield. You're\ntoo young.
MID_SC12_09_m07_002: How are you holding up? I hope you're not worrying\nyour parents.
MID_SC12_09_m07_003: My parents have been dead for a long time. But I'm\nnot looking for your pity.
MID_SC12_09_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m08_001: Yeah...this girl doesn't seem to be as wicked as\nwe'd thought.
MID_SC12_09_m08_002: Which means the problem isn't with her,\nbut someone in her circle.
MID_SC12_09_m09: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m09_001: OK. Let's do this right.
MID_SC12_09_m10: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m10_001: Bucephalus, you're hurt! I'm so sorry...
MID_SC12_09_m10_002: I'll take it from here. You can step back for now.
MID_SC12_09_m11: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_m11_001: I can't go any further. I need to call this what it is.\nA true defeat.
MID_SC12_09_m11_002: Haaah... Haaah...
MID_SC12_09_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_e02_001: That defensive magic is formidable! We shall not\npierce it easily.
MID_SC12_09_e02_002: If we {SetColor=Gold}defeat {SetColor=Default}the {SetColor=Gold}three priests{SetColor=Default} working their magic,\nwe can probably {SetColor=Gold}weaken{SetColor=Default} that defense.
MID_SC12_09_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_e03_001: They're targeting the priests? Everyone, please\nbe careful!
MID_SC12_09_e04: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_e04_001: Another priest?! I won't stand for that. I must\nsupport them!
MID_SC12_09_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_09_e05_001: Thank you for helping me. I swear to avenge you all!
MID_SC12_09_e05_002: Her defensive magic has dissipated. Our attacks will\naffect her.
MID_SC12_10_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m01_001: Don't forget what we're here to do, Nathan.
MID_SC12_10_m01_002: You take care of it. Keep me out of it.
MID_SC12_10_m01_003: Fine. But I need to know I can rely on you to watch\nmy back.
MID_SC12_10_m01_004: Well, now that that's settled, let's get to it. The king\nis watching.
MID_SC12_10_m01_005: Ah!
MID_SC12_10_m01_006: Those two are up to something...
MID_SC12_10_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m02_001: Whaaat?! The priest lady is so...so...PRETTY!
MID_SC12_10_m02_002: She may be pretty...but she's got nothing on Sweetie!
MID_SC12_10_m02_003: Just so. Do not get a swelled head.
MID_SC12_10_m02_004: Oh, my! I guess I should feel flattered...
MID_SC12_10_m02_005: But this is...a problem for me. Credna himself made\nme promise to never reveal my face.
MID_SC12_10_m02_006: No sense worrying now that the cat's out of the bag.\nNothing left to do but see this through.
MID_SC12_10_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m03_001: Startling the elephants into stampeding. Well played.
MID_SC12_10_m03_002: What confusion! How wonderful. This is how battles\nare meant to be!
MID_SC12_10_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m04_001: My, what beauty. Want to leave the battlefield and\nstart our happily ever after?
MID_SC12_10_m04_002: What an offer! Haha... But you're no gentleman—\nstriking at my face like that.
MID_SC12_10_m04_003: Priest lady, are...are you OK? I've never heard\nyou talk like this.
MID_SC12_10_m04_004: She has it right. I am—ever so slightly—extremely\nunhappy with you right now.
MID_SC12_10_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m05_001: Come at me when you wish. I will show you what a\nknight of Arago is capable of.
MID_SC12_10_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m06_001: I wish I could wash my hands of this business. Ah\nwell. This is a contest, and I won't shy away from it.
MID_SC12_10_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m07_001: My, my... I'm sure you had your reasons, but I can't\nimagine keeping such beauty hidden away.
MID_SC12_10_m07_002: Though, your face does remind me of someone I've\nmet in my travels... If only I could remember who...
MID_SC12_10_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m08_001: Your intensity, your strength... There's something\nabout you...
MID_SC12_10_m08_002: It's almost like... What is it... Like you're someone\nI know that I'm scared of.
MID_SC12_10_m08_003: I have heard something similar from another who\nreminds me of you. She said I was like her father.
MID_SC12_10_m08_004: Father, you say? Hmm...
MID_SC12_10_m08_005: What's this all about? You two are getting\nawfully chummy!
MID_SC12_10_m08_006: Irksome, isn't it? My guts twist with it.
MID_SC12_10_m08_007: Is this jealousy? Ridiculous! I, jealous? Ha!
MID_SC12_10_m09: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_m09_001: Well, there it is. You're quite something, to best us.\nWhat do you say, Nathan?
MID_SC12_10_m09_002: We did try. It seems the land has great warriors yet.
MID_SC12_10_e01: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e01_001: That our enemies are seasoned soldiers is bad\nenough, but with war elephants? Tread carefully.
MID_SC12_10_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e02_001: I have an idea! {SetColor=Gold}Destroying that bell tower{SetColor=Default} might\ncreate enough chaos to {SetColor=Gold}confuse their elephants{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC12_10_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e03_001: Listen up! If you see an opportunity, aim for the\nbell tower.
MID_SC12_10_e04: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e04_001: I favor a head-on assault. But I will remember your\nwords. Now, let us fight!
MID_SC12_10_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e05_001: What a good idea! Let's target that during the fight!
MID_SC12_10_e06: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e06_001: Damn. I need to bring that tower down, but these\nelephants are in the way...
MID_SC12_10_e07: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e07_001: If we can lure the war elephants away, it should be\neasier to destroy the bell tower!
MID_SC12_10_e08: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e08_001: We'll have an easier time with the bell tower if we\ncan lure the elephants away...
MID_SC12_10_e09: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e09_001: Lure them? Surely we should simply end them.
MID_SC12_10_e10: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e10_001: <DLG>The bell tower has been destroyed.
MID_SC12_10_e11: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e11_001: Ha! I knew that would work! The elephants are so\nspooked, they can't tell friend from foe.
MID_SC12_10_e12: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e12_001: Looks like the rest of their cavalry is reeling too.\nNow's our chance!
MID_SC12_10_e13: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e13_001: The burden on the soldiers is heavy. The Twin\nJewels of Arago must act.
MID_SC12_10_e14: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e14_001: The battle lines have been thrown into disarray... We\nTwin Jewels have no choice but to step in.
MID_SC12_10_e15: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e15_001: I can't tear my eyes off this battle! Now, come on!\nI want to see blood!
MID_SC12_10_e16: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e16_001: <DLG>Spectators have thrown items into the arena.
MID_SC12_10_e17: <TH>
MID_SC12_10_e17_001: Damn it, looks like the elephants have come to\ntheir senses...
MID_BD12_11_m01: <TH>
MID_BD12_11_m01_001: You wanna go toe-to-toe with me? Heheheh.\nYou're crazy and stupid.
MID_BD12_11_m02: <TH>
MID_BD12_11_m02_001: Right, right. My phantom thread doesn't work on\nthis guy. Annoying. But I'll still win!
MID_BD12_11_m03: <TH>
MID_BD12_11_m03_001: You bastard... At least I still have this...
MID_SC12_12_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m01_001: At last! We are reunited. I am glad.
MID_SC12_12_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m01_002: This is Cetus? The Sea Tyrant? It's enormous! Sea\nbeasts have nothing on this.
MID_SC12_12_m01_003: We'd better get ready. This is no joke.
MID_SC12_12_m01_004: I see... So this is the way of it.
MID_SC12_12_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m02_001: Dietrich, during the journey, I prepared a number of\ntraps for our use.
MID_SC12_12_m02_002: They will ensnare Cetus, so make use of them.
MID_SC12_12_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m03_001: I have waited for this. I have waited so long!
MID_SC12_12_m03_002: I will stake my life on this battle. It is a worthy one!
MID_SC12_12_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m04_001: Upon close examination, it does appear to be a\nsubspecies of dragon. I suspected as much.
MID_SC12_12_m04_002: Though something about it is...different. It is not\nlike the dragons I know well.
MID_SC12_12_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m05_001: The mark on its head... It's the same as my dad's...
MID_SC12_12_m05_002: Cetus... Who are you?
MID_SC12_12_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m06_001: Well! This is a bigger fight than I had imagined.
MID_SC12_12_m06_002: But I say bring it on! I am Mikaela Redblade,\nafter all!
MID_SC12_12_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_m07_001: RRRAAARGH!
MID_SC12_12_e01: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_e01_002: It is larger yet than I imagined. The first thing is to\nobserve its behavior.
MID_SC12_12_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_e02_001: Be careful—it intends to leap! Quick, {SetColor=Gold}get out of the\nway{SetColor=Default} of {SetColor=Gold}where it will land{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC12_12_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_e05_001: The magic trap is operational. We need only ensnare\nour foe.
MID_SC12_12_e08: <TH>
MID_SC12_12_e08_001: <DLG>The magic trap is no longer effective.
MID_BD12_13_m01: <TH>
MID_BD12_13_m01_001: What is this? I've never seen anything like it!
MID_BD12_13_m01_002: Is it a machine? No... Perhaps it would be best to\nterm it a living weapon.
MID_BD12_13_m01_003: Highly vexing, how it bars our path.
MID_BD12_13_m02: <TH>
MID_BD12_13_m02_001: A snake? A worm? No matter. It will soon die.
MID_BD12_13_m02_002: I will run it through and we shall see what happens.
MID_BD12_13_m03: <TH>
MID_BD12_13_m03_001: This foe is unfamiliar to me. We must determine the\nbest course of attack.
MID_BD12_13_m03_002: I had hoped for an uneventful journey. But what fun\nwould that be?
MID_BD12_13_m04: <TH>
MID_BD12_13_m04_001: Hrk... Erk... Ugh...
MID_BD12_13_m05: <TH>
MID_BD12_13_m05_001: It's over. Finally. Now wasn't that creepy?
MID_BD12_13_m05_002: We're getting closer to our destination. And this just\nslowed us down...
MID_BD12_13_m05_003: I've got goosebumps!
MID_BD12_13_m05_004: Do you posit that some unseen hand placed the\nmonster here to hinder us?
MID_SC12_14_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m01_001: Combat in the desert is tricky. Got to watch\nyour footing.
MID_SC12_14_m01_002: Visibility is poor too. It's hard to even find your foe.
MID_SC12_14_m01_003: This is a mess. We'd better be careful.
MID_SC12_14_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m02_001: The {SetColor=Gold}sandstorm{SetColor=Default} obscures our vision. It is best to\npresume it is artificial, and induced by Nuwa.
MID_SC12_14_m02_002: While it has sustained major damage, it is a\nSerpent-Series Craft. We may well be thwarted.
MID_SC12_14_m02_003: Having said that, I have {SetColor=Gold}devices that ought to help\ncounteract the effect{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC12_14_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m03_001: Ignore how they're outfitted and it's obvious they\naren't soldiers. They're amateurs.
MID_SC12_14_m03_002: I don't like being forced to fight them.
MID_SC12_14_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m04_001: Don't let them get any closer! We have to keep\nthem out!
MID_SC12_14_m04_002: If you do not wish to die, clear a path. If you stand in\nmy way, there will be no mercy.
MID_SC12_14_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m05_001: Get out of here, you! Stay out of our village!
MID_SC12_14_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m06_001: Why couldn't you just leave us in peace?
MID_SC12_14_m06_002: Two reasons. One is my mission, of course, but the\nsecond is personal curiosity.
MID_SC12_14_m06_003: You know that I can't trust a word you speak.
MID_SC12_14_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m07_001: I bear you no ill will. But our village must stay secret.
MID_SC12_14_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_m08_001: Our destiny reaches its conclusion... Forgive\nme, Anatolia...
MID_SC12_14_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_e03_001: Go, Titanus! Destroy them!
MID_SC12_14_e04: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_e04_002: A Titanus? Well, one won't pose much of a threat,\nI suppose.
MID_SC12_14_e04_003: However, if they manage to bring forth a large force,\nthat will be another story. Stop them—quickly.
MID_SC12_14_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_e05_002: How irritating that we must hunt them down! Still,\nwe cannot do otherwise if we are to attain victory.
MID_SC12_14_e07: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_e07_001: <DLG>Quell Sandstorm recharges in {Variable=0} {SingularPlural0=turn|turns}.
MID_SC12_14_e08: <TH>
MID_SC12_14_e08_001: <DLG>Quell Sandstorm can be used again.
MID_SC12_15_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_m01_001: I have nothing more to say to you.
MID_SC12_15_m01_002: I am unperturbed. We will have time for a leisurely\nchat after your defeat.
MID_SC12_15_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_m02_001: I would see the power you have attained. Show me.
MID_SC12_15_m02_002: I do not take commands. I will defeat you of my\nown volition.
MID_SC12_15_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_m03_001: As Mediator, I will see your end.
MID_SC12_15_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_m04_001: I... I fall here? In this place?
MID_SC12_15_m04_002: I have failed. I have failed in my mission...
MID_SC12_15_m04_003: Master Long... Zenon... Everyone, I'm so, so sorry...
MID_SC12_15_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e02_001: Two large Titanus? But they are starved of magic\nand will not activate!
MID_SC12_15_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e03_001: Aha! Batteries supply them with magical energy. Our\nfoes intend to use them to make up their shortfall.
MID_SC12_15_e03_002: We simply turn the tables, then. Be sure to {SetColor=Gold}activate\nthe Titanus {SetColor=Default}quickly—{SetColor=Gold}before they do{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC12_15_e04: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e04_001: Why? What difference does it make who\nactivates them?
MID_SC12_15_e04_002: If we do, we can tamper with the batteries and {SetColor=Gold}lower\nthe output {SetColor=Default}of the Titanus. It will give us an edge!
MID_SC12_15_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e05_001: We need more magic if this is going to work. Time to\nactivate the batteries!
MID_SC12_15_e10: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e10_001: No... I can't let things end like this!
MID_SC12_15_e11: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e11_001: I'll throw everything I have at them!
MID_SC12_15_e12: <TH>
MID_SC12_15_e12_001: I'll use my own magic to power up the Titanus!
MID_SC12_16_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m01_001: To see you tremble with joy like this, when most\nbattles see you as placid as an icy pond...
MID_SC12_16_m01_002: Though we have traveled together for half a year by\nnow, this...is new.
MID_SC12_16_m01_003: The only thing reflected in your eyes is that man. He\nhas captured you, and you are transfixed.
MID_SC12_16_m01_004: How I envy you, White-Maned Demon. How I\nenvy you.
MID_SC12_16_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m02_001: Dietrich...your depths are truly boundless.
MID_SC12_16_m02_002: Me? Captivated by him, you say? Me?
MID_SC12_16_m02_003: Oh!
MID_SC12_16_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m03_001: Lay bare your soul, White-Maned Demon, that we\nmay be enraptured by battle!
MID_SC12_16_m03_002: I'm not here to be...enraptured. There's something\nI'm fighting for, and you won't tear it away.
MID_SC12_16_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m04_001: That book The Rise of the White-Maned Demon had\nme hooked!
MID_SC12_16_m04_002: And now I know it's all true, just seeing you here. It's\nan honor to fight you.
MID_SC12_16_m04_003: That's discomfiting. I don't know what to say to that.
MID_SC12_16_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m05_001: I'm sorry. I have my own wish to fulfill.
MID_SC12_16_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m06_001: Ahaha! You are no less exquisite than when I last\nsaw you.
MID_SC12_16_m06_002: A man radiating beauty like a hydrangea cast in\nmoonlight. I must write of you later!
MID_SC12_16_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m07_001: Short by a step. You win, Dietrich.
MID_SC12_16_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_m08_001: You've defeated me... Impressive... I find\nmyself...satisfied.
MID_SC12_16_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_e02_001: The floor is full of {SetColor=Gold}traps{SetColor=Default}. To the left and right are\n{SetColor=Gold}artillery installations{SetColor=Default}. We must act with due caution.
MID_SC12_16_e03: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_e03_001: Unworried about tricks, I see.
MID_SC12_16_e05: <TH>
MID_SC12_16_e05_001: We'll take this seriously. Everyone, forward!
MID_SC15_15_e01: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e01_001: What are these traps on the ground?
MID_SC15_15_e16: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e01_002: I think we'll have to take control of those levers.
MID_SC15_15_e07: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e07_001: We still have to take down that barrier. Let's get to\nthe other levers.
MID_SC15_15_e09: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e09_001: To wait is dull! Shall I join the fray?
MID_SC15_15_e10: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e10_001: I didn't expect their leader to charge in like that.\nUnpredictable, this one. Take caution.
MID_SC15_15_e11: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e11_001: Well done. I look forward to a time when we\ncan duel.
MID_SC15_15_e12: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e12_001: I don't think we've seen all he's capable of... I do not\nlook forward to seeing him again.
MID_SC15_15_e13: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e13_001: And now we may have a serious fight.
MID_SC15_15_e15: <TH>
MID_SC15_15_e15_001: <DLG>A spectator has thrown an item into the arena.
MID_SC12_17_m01: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m01_001: The gods have granted us a superlative matchup this\nday! I know one and all have awaited it hungrily.
MID_SC12_17_m01_002: For a man to challenge a god, and the god to accept...\nit is unprecedented in our glorious history!
MID_SC12_17_m01_003: None can predict the outcome of this battle, the likes\nof which has never been seen!
MID_SC12_17_m01_004: Now, everyone... Breathe deep and steel yourselves...
MID_SC12_17_m01_005: For it is time. We will gaze upon this most\nsingular contest!
MID_SC12_17_m02: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m02_001: The forces Mars has arrayed will prove tricky to rout.
MID_SC12_17_m14: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m02_002: We must remain vigilant against the {SetColor=Gold}priests{SetColor=Default} in the\ncenter. Their {SetColor=Gold}long-range attacks and healing{SetColor=Default}...trouble.
MID_SC12_17_m15: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m02_003: We are surely finished if his forces gain control of the\n{SetColor=Gold}long-range weaponry {SetColor=Default}on either side of the battlefield.
MID_SC12_17_m02_004: Before all else, {SetColor=Gold}seizing it{SetColor=Default} must be the highest priority.
MID_SC12_17_m03: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m03_001: Mars, I have come! Now, give me a true fight!
MID_SC12_17_m03_002: Very well, Dietrich. I will entertain you by bringing\nmy true might to bear!
MID_SC12_17_m04: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m04_001: You face Mars and do not shrink. I commend you!
MID_SC12_17_m05: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m05_001: So you do approach! I will make my move.
MID_SC12_17_m06: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m06_001: I did not foresee that you would make it this far.
MID_SC12_17_m06_002: Your reward will be as ample as your bravery.
MID_SC12_17_m06_003: Look upon the true might of Mars, the Bringer of War!
MID_SC12_17_m07: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m07_001: Rragh!
MID_SC12_17_m07_002: Gods! Mars turned into a dragon! A huge dragon!
MID_SC12_17_m07_003: Mars...I thank you. You have bared your all to me.
MID_SC12_17_m07_004: I must repay this unvarnished truth in kind!
MID_SC12_17_m07_005: Do not come to my aid. I beg you...
MID_SC12_17_m08: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m08_001: It is no small achievement to make Mars respond like\nthis. But the end is nigh for him.
MID_SC12_17_m08_002: Surely there is no way a human can defeat Mars,\na dragon.
MID_SC12_17_m08_003: So you may think, but his fighting spirit\nburns steadily.
MID_SC12_17_m08_004: {SetColor=Gray}What a terrifying creature. I think I understand why\nLyrah was drawn to him.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SC12_17_m09: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m09_001: To see Dietrich so blithely challenge a dragon that\ndwarfs him...
MID_SC12_17_m09_002: It calls the 10 Elites of Fódlan to mind. They were\nno different.
MID_SC12_17_m10: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m10_001: We don't want to get in the way of Dietrich's fight.
MID_SC12_17_m10_002: In fact, let's keep watch for anybody trying to\ninterfere and make sure they never get the chance.
MID_SC12_17_m11: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m11_001: Fearsome dragon! I will wager my very existence to\nface you!
MID_SC12_17_m11_002: That's the way! Fight until your dying breath, man\nfrom another land!
MID_SC12_17_m12: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m12_001: Do not interfere with our noble contest, small one!
MID_SC12_17_m13: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_m13_001: Mars, you brim with the stuff of life... Are you\nunkillable? Is that it?
MID_SC12_17_m13_002: Dietrich! No! If you continue to rail against\nhim, you—
MID_SC12_17_m13_003: You will be consumed by Answerer and become\na beast!
MID_SC12_17_m13_004: The same fate as the warrior Hedda, who vanished\ninto the sea and emerged as Cetus, the Sea Tyrant!
MID_SC12_17_m13_005: Yes, like Maurice of Fódlan, one of the Elites!
MID_SC12_17_e01: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_e01_001: Is this your doing?
MID_SC12_17_e01_002: Yes, it is my stratagem, and it succeeded. You may\nfight as you wish.
MID_SC12_17_e02: <TH>
MID_SC12_17_e02_001: <DLG>Mars's staggering blow made the heal spot unusable.
MID_SC12_XX_Rewind_e01: <TH>
MID_SC12_XX_Rewind_e01_001: Hm? The bag of sand is glowing...